@*
    The show/hide button for a password field. No model — every instance is identical, only its
    position in the markup differs.

    Usage, wrapping the real <input asp-for="..."> exactly where it already sits:

        <div class="auth-password-toggle">
            <input class="auth-field__input" asp-for="Input.Password" ... />
            <partial name="_PasswordToggleButton" />
        </div>

    Deliberately not a partial that takes the input as a model-bound string: asp-for compiles into
    id, name, value AND the unobtrusive-validation data-val-* attributes that asp-validation-for
    reads. Reconstructing that by hand from a raw HTML string would silently drop client-side
    validation. Wrapping the untouched tag helper output keeps all of that intact.

    modules/passwordToggle.ts finds every [data-password-toggle], walks up to this wrapper, and
    flips the sibling <input>'s type between "password" and "text".
*@
<button type="button" class="auth-password-toggle__btn" data-password-toggle
        aria-label="@Loc["Auth.Password.Show"]" aria-pressed="false"
        data-show-label="@Loc["Auth.Password.Show"]" data-hide-label="@Loc["Auth.Password.Hide"]">
    <svg class="auth-password-toggle__icon auth-password-toggle__icon--eye" width="20" height="20"
         viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M1 12s4-7 11-7 11 7 11 7-4 7-11 7-11-7-11-7Z" />
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" />
    </svg>
    <svg class="auth-password-toggle__icon auth-password-toggle__icon--eye-off" width="20" height="20"
         viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M17.94 17.94A10.94 10.94 0 0 1 12 19c-7 0-11-7-11-7a20.3 20.3 0 0 1 4.22-5.06M9.9 4.24A10.4 10.4 0 0 1 12 4c7 0 11 7 11 7a20.3 20.3 0 0 1-2.16 3.19m-6.72-1.07a3 3 0 1 1-4.24-4.24" />
        <path d="M1 1l22 22" />
    </svg>
</button>
